    },
    "message": "Own the population, overlay and config documents in Rust and check them by generation\n\npopulation_presence_v1, population_lifecycle_v1, population_dynamics_v1, temporary_spaces_v1,\ngeometry_overlay_v1 and model_configs become V rows. A mirror's generation changes with every\nwrite that reaches its tree, so TickValidationMemo.begin and the controller's minute start know\nthese are unchanged without encoding 60 KB and comparing 130 KB of JSON. The dynamics check joins\nthe checks skipped while nothing they read changed. Presence history grows in place, since a new\nlist would be converted again record by record, and a waiting list that stays the same is not\nwritten.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
